t:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:right;line-height:normal\" align=\"right\"><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:#cccccc\">2.</span></p>\r\n  </td>\r\n  <td style=\"padding:.75pt .75pt .75pt .75pt\">\r\n  <p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;\">experiment(sim = mySim, replicates = 2, dirPrefix = &quot;exp1&quot;,\r\n  saveExperiment = FALSE, clearSimEnv = FALSE)</span></p>\r\n  </td>\r\n </tr>\r\n</tbody></table>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;line-height:16.5pt\"><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:#eaeaea;display:none\"> </span></p>\r\n\r\n<table cellspacing=\"3\" cellpadding=\"0\" border=\"0\">\r\n <tbody><tr>\r\n  <td style=\"width:.25in;padding:.75pt .75pt .75pt .75pt\" width=\"27\" valign=\"top\" nowrap>\r\n  <p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:.05in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-left:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:right;line-height:normal\" align=\"right\"><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:#cccccc\">1.</span></p>\r\n  </td>\r\n  <td style=\"padding:.75pt .75pt .75pt .75pt\">\r\n  <p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;\">experiment(sim = mySim, replicates = 2, dirPrefix = &quot;exp1&quot;,\r\n  saveExperiment = FALSE, clearSimEnv = FALSE)</span></p>\r\n  </td>\r\n </tr>\r\n</tbody></table>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span> </span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span>It appears that information\r\nwithin one of my raster objects ‘vegMapInit’ is not being accessed correctly\r\nduring the crop function in one of my modules, when I use the experiment function.\r\n</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span>sim$vegMap &lt;-<span>  </span>crop(sim$vegMapInit, studyAreaTmp)</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span>If I ask for table(sim$vegMapInit[])\r\nI get the following error message: </span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span lang=\"FR-CA\">Error: cannot allocate vector of size\r\n1.6 Gb</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span> </span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span>My understanding is\r\nthat the crop function is managing to access and select only the information\r\nthat is required from vegMapInit when the simulation is run independently, but\r\nsomehow it is unable to do this when it is run through the experiment function,\r\ntries to select everything, and becomes overwhelmed. Could this be the case?\r\nWhy would this be? </span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span> </span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span>Thank you!</span></p>\r\n\r\n</div>"
